Maintainer wording: start unreagent in a freshly created Unreal project and say "set up the rest" — the agent builds a good setup from what it sees and knows, and asks where it cannot tell.

Content: how to inspect the project (C++ or Blueprint-only, engine version, plugins present, source control); verify launcher, editor and toolkit; run init / write unreagent.yaml; add the toolkit (exact command, which branch for 5.8); first compile via unreagent-build; then the Claude-side setup for the game project — a CLAUDE.md describing the project, and agents and skills where the project is large enough to need them; which questions to ask the human (genre and scope, target platforms, C++ vs Blueprint policy, source control, Fab content wanted) and which to answer from the tree. Points to unreagent-build, unreagent-iterate and the Fab skill; does not restate them.

Open for the planner before writing: how much of the agent-team setup this skill carries itself versus pointing at a public kit, and whether unreagent materializes anything into .claude/ beyond the skills it already ships.

Maintainer decision, 2026-11-22: Blueprint-only projects are out of scope — the projects carry plugins and are C++ projects anyway. The skill assumes a C++ project and does not describe a Blueprint-only path.

